model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "The disabled runtime-slot controller owns active selection in runtime-slots-v1 storage beside existing ownership and membership records. The live stack evaluates no extra resource, exports no runtime class, and adds no binding, migration or release declaration. A future private slot driver must bind provider application, version, logical instance, immutable image and process boot separately from the stable controller identity. Candidate startup never calls the active runtime lifecycle. Promotion collects fresh health and every current clean native-policy acknowledgement outside storage transactions, then compares complete membership and selection in one transaction and commits selection with its receipt. Expired candidate acknowledgements cannot borrow a renewed desired deadline. An uncertain started promotion permits inspection only. Admission leases register before authority or signing and identify their selected slot before dispatch. Revocation persists dirty state and aborts pool streams before all active, candidate and draining slots acknowledge, or an explicit durable controller fence denies routing and closes that slot's streams. An unknown or unfenced non-acknowledging slot prevents writer acknowledgement. Drivers have no public ingress. Per-slot health leases protect draining streams independently. Retirement waits for drain, targets the exact old boot and retains uncertainty without repeating destruction. At most one inactive candidate or draining slot coexists with active serving. Switching back requires the same fresh policy and identity proof. Existing lifecycle code ignores the additive namespace. Provisioning, private runtime adapters, release admission and live reliance require their separate approved phase."
      bindings "this.deps.driver=basalt.poolRuntime"
    }
  }
}
